Package: rpython
Type: Package
Title: High-Level, Bidirectional, Semantic Interoperability Between R and 'Python'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Merwan", "Roudane", email = "merwanroudane920@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: The R companion of the 'RPython' platform. Runs R as an isolated worker for
    the 'Python' package of the same name and, symmetrically, drives a 'Python' worker from
    R ('python()'). Objects cross the boundary through a portable semantic envelope
    (JSON plus Apache Arrow IPC files) that preserves types, missing-value semantics,
    factor levels and ordering, time zones, time-series frequency, panel structure,
    survey labels, geometries and coordinate reference systems, sparse storage, graph
    topology and more; objects without a lossless representation stay native behind
    proxies. No data is copied for database relations and file-backed rasters.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
